    §2__\\§4;_§2\\//___

 A Saga Of Mysteries
#-  §d╔═--═ஓ๑♣๑ஓ═--═╗
      §5Witch-Craft?
 §d╚═--═ஓ๑♣๑ஓ═--═╝

Dear Diary,
The anomaly we have named 'The Sinkhole' has been on my radar since I first set foot here on this island. Like a siren's call...

I'd been eagerly waiting for when the 
#- §dDeathcap Team would show up at my tavern doorstep, and they did. Both MissPortinari, (The CEO) and Dr. Link, armed to the teeth with investigation equipment and climbing gear. Together we carefully ventured into the depths. Every step felt so wrong yet... so right! Personally because
#- §dI'm attuned to any high energy, I could already sense the air around us changing. One minute thick and heavy, the next light as a feather. Missp noticed how both fresh and rotting nature, stone and dirt melted into each other seamlessly. I took notes in my Grimoire. Dr. Link took notes in
#- §dher laptop which I thought looked impractical and awkward. She saw glowing eyes looking at her through the screen and nearly ran headfirst into a stalactite. Missp's EMF meter went mental and at one point I swear I heard the beeps play the melody of 'spooky scary skeletons'.
#- §dAs we all descended into the darkness, none of us could shake the feeling of unease. Missp nearly called off the whole thing, but not before me eye's snapped towards an old metal box stuck inside some rock. It's presence both alluring and foreboding. Hours went by as we dug 
#- §dthe box out. It was beaten up but remained strong. "§2This has your name written all over it Sweetpea§d" Dr. Link exclaimed. "§6Yeah very funny, blame the strange stuff on the witch...§d" I scoffed. "§2No, I mean, this box literally has your name on it...§d". We all stood in shock for a while as Dr. Links
#- §dUV light revealed my name scratched all over the silver metal. 

When we snapped out of it, Missp held the box up towards me. When I lifted the lid and beheld the contents within, my heart skipped a beat. Books, magazines, brand new, untouched. All named; Witch-Craft. 
#- §dEach page contained writings that mirrored my own, yet I have no memory of ever penning such works. How is it possible that these books exist? 
Is this some kind of twisted joke? 
Someone's fanfiction? 
   Who 
         is     §5ɨȶ§d?
My mind almost burst with visions, a deep
#- §dinner knowing and un-knowing in my bones. Was this a rift in the fabric of reality? Or just 
in my own reality?

As we all grappled with these unsettling questions, we knew The Sinkhole held more than just answers. With our curiosity piqued we
#- §dall vowed to investigate further. And I would devote my time to studying these Witch-Craft Magazines and unravel the enigma. 

Each night, instead of rest, I pour over these pages, searching for clues, for answers that escape my grasp.
#- §dThey haunt my every thought. I find myself consumed. An insatiable obsession.
The story, so familiar yet foreign, taunting me. The others already voiced their concerns. Can't stop. 

Why else did you 
think I continued this magazine... 
           §odear reader§r?
#-        §6Sweetpea's§r
